    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0114" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg34"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Finding that the inclosed communication of
                    the Neue Wiener Tagblatt from a correspondent in New York had escaped the
                    attention of the consul-general here, I have the honor to transmit it herewith
                    for the information of the Department, believing that it contains sufficient
                    matter of interest, especially as it pertains to the method of the customs
                    officials in New York in applying and interpreting the tariff laws.</p>
                <p>It is important that the consular officers in the United States should lose no
                    opportunity to counteract the effect of such statements as are made in this
                    article and contradict them when not in accordance with the fact.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d32-a1.xml" xpointer="d32-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
